-- title:
--   The shifted permutation's support and the negative-extreme level set partition all positions
-- statement:
--   The shifted permutation's support and the negative-extreme level set partition all positions.
--
--   Let $n>0$ and write $I_n=\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z$, represented by $0,\ldots,n-1$. The symbol $\operatorname{rep}$ takes a residue to its nonnegative representative and leaves ordinary integers unchanged. Residue sums and differences are cyclic; inequalities use representatives. $\mathfrak S(I_n)$ is the permutation group. Function symbols are written in curried notation; a subscript $\#$ means finite cardinality. $\mathrm{Lift}(p,c,d)$ means $\sum_i d(i)=0$ and $i+d(i)\equiv p^{-1}(i)+c\pmod n$ for every residue $i$. $\mathrm{Shift}(p,c,h)(i)=p^{-1}(i)+c+h$ modulo $n$. $\operatorname{supp}(p)$ is the moved-point set and $\operatorname{cycles}(p)$ its nontrivial disjoint cycle factors; cycle membership includes fixed singleton orbits.
--
--   The precise quantified assertion, with all its hypotheses, is
--
--   $$
--   \forall  (n : \mathbb N_{>0}) (p : \mathfrak S(I_n)) (c : \mathbb Z) (d : I_{n} \to  \mathbb Z), \operatorname{Lift} p c d \to  \forall  (h : \mathbb Z), (\forall  (i : I_{n}), 0 \le  d i + h \land  d i + h < \operatorname{rep}\,n) \to  (\operatorname{supp} (\operatorname{Shift} p c h))_{\#} + \{i\mid d i = -h\}_{\#} = n
--   $$
--
--   This identity can be used while tracking the exact cost or structure of the sorting construction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/StrictBandEquality.lean#L57-L73

